 "structural_change": "mu2 (coordinator 10-19: register every tile pin by default; cycles are cheap) of qkd_kvs_ctl_mu1 (MU 1 release view, ROOT-RST reset landing 2 stages): (1) PIN REGISTERS ON, all faces (recipe 3, +1 ck on every registered input and output crossing of kvs_ctl; ck / rst_n / por_n excluded as clock / landed resets) -- p1-d7af727c1 had ~1,580 IO endpoints at -0.25..-0.5 ns TT (port -> child flop wires across the 475 um tile, pin regs opted out); (2) boot dispatcher SRQ=2: setup_ready = the combinational term 2 edges later (stage 1 internal 160-applied/installed/seal reduction and pin terms registered separately, stage 2 AND) -- p1 in->out boot_image_target -> setup_ready -698 ps; (3) ownership calendar PIPE=1: drained_all_q = &drained_q one edge later and root-k offsets captured with the root words -- p1 reg2reg -487 ps = drained_q -> wire (~230 ps buffers) -> 32-AND (OR4/OR5 x4 levels) -> 32-b subtract+compare -> bad -> enable of ~140 root flops: DEPTH + wire, not fanout (no net > 32 sinks on the path).  Schedule: drain guard observed 1 ck earlier before enter / leave; setup_ready +2 ck; every kvs_ctl crossing +1 ck (die ages, MU-DIE-KV). Tile file qkd_kvs_tiles_hroot_ff_k_mu.sv regenerated (kv_static.py ownership PIPE=1 / kv_static_boot_join SRQ=2 under OT_KV_MU=1; ports / outline / pins unchanged vs mu1).  lprg_mu (MU-KV-BOOT) not ready: not included.",
